{
  "id": "eval-number-string-is-wrong-type",
  "description": "Pin engine behaviour: a string fact compared to a numeric rule value is treated as 'present-but-wrong-type → false' (rule-model.md §5.1). The rule does not match. Companion to eval-number-int-float-equivalence: prevents the engine from later quietly coercing strings to numbers, which would be a surprising behaviour change for callers that rely on the strict-type contract.",
  "ruleset": {
    "schema_version": "1.0",
